# Imported labeled documents, actual shared local dispatch, no live provider.
name: Accept exact Map context and retain it through a fixed study and restart
size: 120x36
cwd: @TMP_TARGET
env-unset: ANTHROPIC_API_KEY OPENAI_API_KEY NO_COLOR KUZUSHI_SKIP_ONBOARDING
env: HOME=@TMP_HOME KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1
require-shell: python3 @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/map_context.py @TMP_TARGET @ART seed
launch: --target @TMP_TARGET
require-live-snap: 30 KUZUSHI | ready
paste-file: @ART/alpha-command.txt
keys: Enter
require-live-snap: 30 RESULT READY | imported
require-live-snap: 25 Alpha receiver | reviewing-map
expect: RESULT READY
expect-not: Beta receiver
require-shell: python3 @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/map_context.py @TMP_TARGET @ART reviewing
ask: Does Map show the exact imported Alpha context for review while the globally active Beta remains unchanged?
nav-mode:
keys: u
require-live-snap: 20 Viewing Scan | after-acceptance
require-shell: python3 @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/map_context.py @TMP_TARGET @ART accepted
submit: map
require-live-snap: 20 accepted | accepted-map
ask: Does acceptance advance to Scan while returning to Map preserves the approved picture and clearly names its accepted state?
keys: Tab
require-live-snap: 15 DATA-FLOW DIAGRAM | exact-dfd
expect-not: Beta receiver
ask: Does the DFD show the accepted context, with legible topology and useful keyboard controls?
resize: 80x24
require-live-snap: 15 Alpha client | map-80
ask: Is the exact DFD readable at 80x24 without hiding navigation?
resize: 60x20
require-live-snap: 15 Alpha client | map-60
ask: Does the Map flow remain readable at 60x20?
resize: 40x12
require-live-snap: 15 Alpha client | map-40
expect: Alpha client
ask: Are Map navigation and inspection still usable at 40x12?
nav-mode:
keys: j
require-live-snap: 15 Alpha receiver | map-40-selected
ask: Does keyboard selection reveal the selected component at 40x12 instead of spending the only reading row on a border?
keys: k
resize: 96x89
require-live-snap: 15 Alpha client | map-tall
ask: Does the tall layout retain a clear hierarchy and exact context evidence?
resize: 160x48
require-live-snap: 15 Alpha client | map-wide
ask: Does the wide layout show a useful DFD without stretched copy or lost controls?
resize: 120x36
keys: Escape
submit: use sast
submit: options sast:scan
submit: set taskMode manual
submit: set tasks secret-scan
submit: scan batch
require-live-snap: 25 PLAN A STUDY | study-form
keys: L
require-live-snap: 30 Draft ready | exact-study
require-shell: python3 @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/map_context.py @TMP_TARGET @ART study
ask: Does the three-pass plan retain accepted Alpha context without launching work or implying approval?
keys: Down Down Down Enter
require-live-snap: 20 Enter inspect | plan-context-choice
keys: Enter
require-live-snap: 25 CONTEXT SUMMARY | plan-context-inspected
expect: Labeled diagram Alpha
expect-not: Labeled diagram Beta
require-shell: python3 @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/map_context.py @TMP_TARGET @ART study
ask: Does exact plan-context inspection show accepted Alpha and its grounding limitations while preserving the draft and active Beta?
keys: Escape
require-live-snap: 15 PLAN A STUDY | returned-study
keys: Escape
require-live-snap: 15 KUZUSHI | returned-origin
keys: C-c
require-exit: 10
env: HOME=@TMP_HOME KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1 NO_COLOR=1
launch: --target @TMP_TARGET
require-live-snap: 30 KUZUSHI | restarted
submit: map
require-live-snap: 20 Alpha receiver | resumed-map
expect-not: Beta receiver
require-shell: python3 @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/map_context.py @TMP_TARGET @ART resumed
ask: Does a fresh no-color process restore the accepted exact Map and preserve honest scan-plan state?
require-shell: python3 @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/map_context.py @TMP_TARGET @ART remove
keys: C-c
require-exit: 10
env: HOME=@TMP_HOME KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1 NO_COLOR=1
launch: --target @TMP_TARGET
require-live-snap: 30 KUZUSHI | missing-restart
submit: map
require-live-snap: 25 Recorded Map context unavailable | missing-map
expect-not: Beta receiver
expect-not: Alpha receiver
require-shell: python3 @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/map_context.py @TMP_TARGET @ART missing
ask: Does a missing accepted object stop the DFD from silently showing another model and explain the unavailable evidence?
resize: 40x12
require-live-snap: 15 Recorded Map context unavailable | missing-map-40
expect: Enter inspect Map runs
ask: Does the smallest missing-context state explain the problem and keep run inspection reachable?
nav-mode:
keys: Enter
require-live-snap: 15 JOBS | missing-inspection
require-shell: python3 @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/map_context.py @TMP_TARGET @ART missing
ask: Does Enter inspect recorded Map runs without starting replacement work or activating another model?
keys: C-c
require-exit: 10
